  "narrative": {
    "key_bets": [
      "Laser-patterned REBCO film on cylindrical substrates can be manufactured at nuclear-grade quality and 1 m diameter scale, replacing wound-tape coils",
      "Compact (A≈4) quasi-isodynamic stellarator at 10 T can achieve ignited (Q=∞) D-T plasma with no continuous external heating at steady state",
      "Flowing Li-LiH liquid metal wall can sustain 25 MW/m² continuous heat loading while serving as integrated first wall, breeder, shield, and coolant",
      "Integrated blanket achieves TBR = 1.60 with non-enriched natural Li-LiH (10 cm Pb + 22 cm Li-LiH), confirmed by JNM 599 (2024)",
      "sCO₂ Brayton-Rankine combined cycle delivers 49–51% thermal efficiency at GW scale from a liquid metal heat source",
      "HTS magnets at 20 K reach 10 T nominal on-axis with peak coil fields up to 15–40 T despite REBCO Jc degradation above ~20 T",
      "Stellarator steady-state operation with near-100% duty cycle yields ~90–95% plant capacity factor"
    ],
    "eliminated_costs": [
      "No central solenoid or current-drive system required (inherent stellarator advantage)",
      "No continuous heating system at steady state (Q=∞ eliminates ECRH/NBI capital and recirculating load)",
      "No disruption-mitigation hardware (stellarators are disruption-free)",
      "No discrete first-wall replacement cycle (flowing liquid wall replaces solid PFC modules)",
      "No REBCO wound-tape supply chain dependency (laser patterning replaces tape winding)"
    ],
    "novel_costs": [
      "Laser-patterned REBCO thin-film deposition on 1 m diameter cylinders — no industrial cost analogue at any scale (3–10× uncertainty in C220103)",
      "Flowing Li-LiH liquid metal circulation system with pumps, MHD piping, heat exchangers, and tritium extraction (consolidates C220101/C220102 into one pumped-fluid system)",
      "sCO₂ Brayton-Rankine turbomachinery at GW scale with tritium-compatible heat exchangers (TRL 4–5, no demonstrated GW-scale BOP)",
      "High-throughput liquid metal pumping power (~380 MW estimated) to support 25 MW/m² wall loading — 5× higher than solid-blanket designs",
      "Quench detection and protection system for distributed thin-film HTS (fundamentally different from wound-tape protection)"
    ],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "ISS04 confinement scaling predicts n·τ_E ~11× below Lawson threshold at T=10 keV — Q=∞ ignition closure is not supported by current stellarator scaling laws",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Laser-patterned HTS film manufacturing has no industrial cost analogue; 10× cost scenario drives LCOE to ~516 $/MWh (vs. 129 $/MWh nominal)",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Flowing Li-LiH wall at 25 MW/m² has never been demonstrated; MHD stability of free-surface liquid metal in 3D stellarator field is uncharacterized",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Compact A≈4 QI geometry has no stellarator experimental precedent (W7-X is A=10); confinement quality at this aspect ratio is untested",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "REBCO Jc degrades sharply above ~20 T at 20 K, threatening feasibility of 20–40 T peak coil field upper envelope",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Zero published capital cost or LCOE estimate from the company; every CAS account must be built from first principles with no anchor",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Liquid metal circulation pump power undisclosed (~380 MW estimated, ±50%); drives unexplained 32% recirculating fraction between cycle (50%) and net (34%) efficiency",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Plant availability uncertainty — flowing-wall maintenance philosophy uncharacterized; elasticity of −0.94 makes availability the single largest LCOE lever",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "No divertor design or plasma exhaust solution addressed in any published source",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Tritium permeation from liquid Li-LiH primary circuit through sCO₂ heat exchangers is uncharacterized; safety-relevant and may require permeation barriers",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Simultaneous Li-LiH chemical exposure plus 14 MeV neutron irradiation at fusion-relevant fluences not demonstrated for any RAFM structural alloy",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "sCO₂ Brayton-Rankine combined cycle at 49–51% efficiency not demonstrated at GW scale or with liquid metal heat source",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "NNBI startup-only duty cycle is unusual; long-term reliability of intermittent-use NNBI over plant lifetime not characterized",
        "severity": "low"
